{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Hyperparameter Tuning Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: Grid Search from Scratch"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The code in `code/tuning.py` implements grid search, random search, and a simple Bayesian optimizer from scratch."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def grid_search(model_fn, param_grid, X_train, y_train, X_val, y_val):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    keys = list(param_grid.keys())"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    values = list(param_grid.values())"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    best_score = -float(\"inf\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    best_params = None"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    n_evals = 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for combo in itertools.product(*values):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        params = dict(zip(keys, combo))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        model = model_fn(**params)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        model.fit(X_train, y_train)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        score = evaluate(model, X_val, y_val)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        n_evals += 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if score > best_score:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            best_score = score"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            best_params = params"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return best_params, best_score, n_evals"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: Random Search from Scratch"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def random_search(model_fn, param_distributions, X_train, y_train,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                  X_val, y_val, n_iter=50, seed=42):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    rng = np.random.RandomState(seed)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    best_score = -float(\"inf\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    best_params = None"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for _ in range(n_iter):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        params = {k: sample(v, rng) for k, v in param_distributions.items()}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        model = model_fn(**params)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        model.fit(X_train, y_train)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        score = evaluate(model, X_val, y_val)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if score > best_score:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            best_score = score"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            best_params = params"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return best_params, best_score, n_iter"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: Bayesian Optimization (Simplified)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The core idea: fit a Gaussian process to observed (hyperparameter, score) pairs, then use an acquisition function to decide where to look next."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class SimpleBayesianOptimizer:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, search_space, n_initial=5):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.search_space = search_space"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.n_initial = n_initial"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.X_observed = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.y_observed = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def _kernel(self, x1, x2, length_scale=1.0):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        dists = np.sum((x1[:, None, :] - x2[None, :, :]) ** 2, axis=2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return np.exp(-0.5 * dists / length_scale ** 2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def _fit_gp(self, X_new):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        X_obs = np.array(self.X_observed)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        y_obs = np.array(self.y_observed)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        y_mean = y_obs.mean()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        y_centered = y_obs - y_mean"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        K = self._kernel(X_obs, X_obs) + 1e-4 * np.eye(len(X_obs))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        K_star = self._kernel(X_new, X_obs)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        L = np.linalg.cholesky(K)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        alpha = np.linalg.solve(L.T, np.linalg.solve(L, y_centered))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        mu = K_star @ alpha + y_mean"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        v = np.linalg.solve(L, K_star.T)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        var = 1.0 - np.sum(v ** 2, axis=0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        var = np.maximum(var, 1e-6)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return mu, var"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def _expected_improvement(self, mu, var, best_y):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        sigma = np.sqrt(var)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        z = (mu - best_y) / (sigma + 1e-10)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        ei = sigma * (z * norm_cdf(z) + norm_pdf(z))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return ei"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def suggest(self):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if len(self.X_observed) < self.n_initial:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            return sample_random(self.search_space)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        candidates = [sample_random(self.search_space) for _ in range(500)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        X_cand = np.array([to_vector(c) for c in candidates])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        mu, var = self._fit_gp(X_cand)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        ei = self._expected_improvement(mu, var, max(self.y_observed))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return candidates[np.argmax(ei)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def observe(self, params, score):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.X_observed.append(to_vector(params))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.y_observed.append(score)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The GP surrogate gives two things at each candidate point: a predicted score (mu) and an uncertainty (var). Expected Improvement balances these: it favors points where the model predicts high scores OR where uncertainty is high. Early on, most points have high uncertainty so the optimizer explores. Later, it focuses on the most promising region."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: Compare All Methods"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Run all three methods on the same synthetic objective and compare. This comparison uses a simplified wrapper that calls each optimizer with a direct objective function (no model training), so the API differs from the model-based implementations above:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def synthetic_objective(params):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    lr = params[\"learning_rate\"]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    depth = params[\"max_depth\"]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return -(np.log10(lr) + 2) ** 2 - (depth - 4) ** 2 + 10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "param_grid = {"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"learning_rate\": [0.001, 0.01, 0.1, 1.0],"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"max_depth\": [2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8],"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "grid_best = None"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "grid_score = -float(\"inf\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "grid_history = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "for combo in itertools.product(*param_grid.values()):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    params = dict(zip(param_grid.keys(), combo))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    score = synthetic_objective(params)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    grid_history.append((params, score))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if score > grid_score:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        grid_score = score"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        grid_best = params"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "param_dist = {"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"learning_rate\": (\"log_float\", 0.001, 1.0),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"max_depth\": (\"int\", 2, 8),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "rand_best = None"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "rand_score = -float(\"inf\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "rand_history = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "rng = np.random.RandomState(42)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "for _ in range(28):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    params = {k: sample(v, rng) for k, v in param_dist.items()}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    score = synthetic_objective(params)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    rand_history.append((params, score))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if score > rand_score:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        rand_score = score"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        rand_best = params"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "optimizer = SimpleBayesianOptimizer(param_dist, n_initial=5)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "bayes_history = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "for _ in range(28):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    params = optimizer.suggest()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    score = synthetic_objective(params)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    optimizer.observe(params, score)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    bayes_history.append((params, score))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "bayes_score = max(s for _, s in bayes_history)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"{'Method':<20} {'Best Score':>12} {'Evaluations':>12}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(\"-\" * 50)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"{'Grid Search':<20} {grid_score:>12.4f} {len(grid_history):>12}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"{'Random Search':<20} {rand_score:>12.4f} {len(rand_history):>12}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(f\"{'Bayesian Opt':<20} {bayes_score:>12.4f} {len(bayes_history):>12}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "With the same budget, Bayesian optimization usually finds the best score fastest because it does not waste evaluations in clearly bad regions. Random search covers more ground than grid search. Grid search only wins when you have very few hyperparameters and can afford to be exhaustive."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. Run grid search and random search with the same total budget (e.g., 50 evaluations). Compare the best scores found. Run the experiment 10 times with different seeds. How often does random search win?\n\n2. Implement Hyperband from scratch. Start with 81 configurations, each trained for 1 epoch. Keep the top 1/3 at each round and triple their budget. Compare total compute (sum of all epochs across all configs) to running 81 configs for the full budget.\n\n3. Add a learning rate scheduler (cosine annealing) to the gradient boosting implementation from Lesson 11. Does it help compared to a fixed learning rate?\n\n4. Use Optuna to tune a RandomForestClassifier on a real dataset (e.g., sklearn's breast cancer dataset). Use `optuna.visualization.plot_param_importances(study)` to see which hyperparameters matter most. Does it match the importance ranking from this lesson?\n\n5. Implement a simple acquisition function (Expected Improvement) and demonstrate exploration vs exploitation. Plot the surrogate model's mean and uncertainty, and show where EI chooses to evaluate next."
      ]
    }
  ],
